Kellum Quinn is a contemporary painter. He kept his life private, and what is known of him is that he explored both [[Færrin]] and the worlds along the [[Infinite Horizon|horizon]], painting the vistas he came across as he went. He travelled alone. He is in theory still alive, but about five years ago he left on another trek and has not been seen since; he had gone away for long stretches before, and those who know his work do not take his absence for death.

One of his paintings, *Joker World*, hung in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Metropolitan Conservatory|MetCon]] in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], most of the canvas given over to reddish-black smoke rising from a volcano over cracked red clay. Another, *Second Meaning*, a long landscape of the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]] skyline, hung in [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]]'s manor, its paint raised in the middle as if something had been painted over.

*Second Meaning* was taken from [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]]'s manor by the Party and traded to [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]] for keystone 14. When the Heart stripped the paint, the tower hidden under the skyline proved to be the [[Pharos]], painted into the work and covered over.
